(4773512, 683830, 54632, '<td valign="top">Hi,<br/> <br/>I''m just wondering... if you used a 10-22 lens F3.5 - 4.5, how can the aperture in your shot be F2.8?<br/> <br/>Great shot too!<br/> <br/>EDIT: I just realised you mentioned you used a Sigma 24-70 f/2.8 lens.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-17 22:31:25.</i></td>', 'Hi, I''m just wondering... if you used a 10-22 lens F3.5 - 4.5, how can the aperture in your shot be F2.8? Great shot too! EDIT: I just realised you mentioned you used a Sigma 24-70 f/2.8 lens.', '2008-06-17 23:29:41.000000', '2008-06-17 23:31:25.000000', 0),
(4774041, 683287, 34462, '<td valign="top">Love the soft focus and the sense of movement in this photo, and being a father of tow-heads myself, I love the way you captured the light in their hair. Beautiful.<br/></td>', 'Love the soft focus and the sense of movement in this photo, and being a father of tow-heads myself, I love the way you captured the light in their hair. Beautiful.', '2008-06-18 05:39:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4775150, 685380, 68035, '<td valign="top">I am glad this finished so well for you.  One of those images that encapsulates what its like being a boy and having a brother.  next time the kids are bouncing of the walls and driving you crazy its the sort of picture you should just look at and realise that the mayhem is temporary, but the love is forever</td>', 'I am glad this finished so well for you.  One of those images that encapsulates what its like being a boy and having a brother.  next time the kids are bouncing of the walls and driving you crazy its the sort of picture you should just look at and realise that the mayhem is temporary, but the love is forever', '2008-06-18 17:56:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4775165, 683287, 68035, '<td valign="top">In so many ways this brings back memories of the fantastic ''Grace Kelly'' portrait from the side challenge last year<br/> <br/>Its just wonderful to see sisters playing together in this way and its a great mixture of action and stillness (I love Ashley''s expression of normality and calm as her hair flies behind her) and childhood and growing up<br/> <br/>As ever beautifully processed in B&amp;W which really is your oeuvre</td>', 'In so many ways this brings back memories of the fantastic ''Grace Kelly'' portrait from the side challenge last year Its just wonderful to see sisters playing together in this way and its a great mixture of action and stillness (I love Ashley''s expression of normality and calm as her hair flies behind her) and childhood and growing up As ever beautifully processed in B&W which really is your oeuvre', '2008-06-18 18:05:16.000000', NULL, 0),
